  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Suppose a contest has NNN problems, with difficulties A1,A2,...,ANA_1, A_2, ..., A_NA1​,A2​,...,AN​, and we have a parameter XXX. The contest is said to be balanced if and only if the following conditions hold :\n\n\nAi≥Ai−1A_i \\ge A_{i - 1}Ai​≥Ai−1​ for all 2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N, i.e. the problems are sorted in difficulty order.\nAi−Ai−1≤XA_i - A_{i - 1} \\le XAi​−Ai−1​≤X for all 2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N, i.e. the difficulties between 222 adjacent problems differ by at most XXX.\nRight now, your contest has problems of difficulties B1,B2,...,BNB_1, B_2, ..., B_NB1​,B2​,...,BN​. You sorted them in difficulty order, so Bi≥Bi−1B_i \\ge B_{i - 1}Bi​≥Bi−1​ holds.\n\nYou want to modify the problems to ensure that the contest becomes balanced. Suppose the final contest difficulties were C1,C2,...,CNC_1, C_2, ..., C_NC1​,C2​,...,CN​. Then, the cost of this contest is max⁡i=1N(∣Ci−Bi∣)\\max_{i = 1}^{N}(|C_i - B_i|)maxi=1N​(∣Ci​−Bi​∣). Minimize the cost while achieving a balanced contest. It can be proven that a balanaced contest always exists. Please note that problems are even allowed to have negative difficulties.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN and XXX - the size of the array and the parameter.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,...,BNB_1, B_2, ..., B_NB1​,B2​,...,BN​\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\n\noutput on a new  line : KKK the minimum cost of a balanced contest\n\n\n\n\noutput on the next line : NNN integers, C1,C2,...,CNC_1, C_2, ..., C_NC1​,C2​,...,CN​ representing a balanced contest acheiveing the minimum cost KKK. The following conditions should hold for CCC :\n\n\n\n−2⋅109≤Ci≤2⋅109- 2 \\cdot 10^9 \\le C_i \\le 2 \\cdot 10^9−2⋅109≤Ci​≤2⋅109\nCi≥Ci−1C_i \\ge C_{i - 1}Ci​≥Ci−1​\nCi−Ci−1≤XC_i - C_{i - 1} \\le XCi​−Ci−1​≤X\n\n\n\nIf several such contests exists, output any.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Bi,X≤1091 \\le B_i, X \\le 10^91≤Bi​,X≤109",
      "Bi≥Bi−1B_i \\ge B_{i - 1}Bi​≥Bi−1​",
      "The sum of NNN over all tests does not exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105"
    ],
